cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pdb_align: protein structure alignment and prediction-model assessment"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it, and cite the
  original papers for whichever metrics you report (listed under references
  below and in docs/METHODS.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zyla
    given-names: Dawid
    affiliation: University of Colorado Anschutz Medical Campus
version: 0.4.1
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/dzyla/pdb_align"
keywords:
  - structural biology
  - protein structure alignment
  - TM-score
  - lDDT
  - DockQ
  - AlphaFold
  - epitope mapping
abstract: >-
  pdb_align compares protein structures and scores predicted models against
  experimental references. It provides sequence-guided and sequence-free
  superposition, automatic multi-chain correspondence, flexible (multi-domain)
  alignment, and the standard assessment metrics — TM-score, GDT_TS, lDDT-Ca,
  DockQ with its CAPRI classes, epitope/paratope agreement, pDockQ and pDockQ2
  — as a Python API, a command-line tool and a web front-end. Metric
  implementations are cross-validated against the reference programs (DockQ,
  TM-align) in the test suite, and each reported number states what it was
  normalized by.
